            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0295" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89Rumania/55: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-04-06T12:00:00+01:44"><hi rendition="#italic">April 6,
                                1925—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 11:49 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>29.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>It is my personal impression, which I should like to have officially confirmed as
                    far as possible through the Rumanian Legation in Washington, that the Rumanian
                    Government, in despair at failures in the European markets, is making a sincere
                    bid for American financial support, with corresponding advantages to us. For
                    this reason I do not recommend too vigorous action at present, as at last the
                    Government seems to realize absolute necessity of obtaining our good will.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
